  nonce: 29b9  # 29b9
  message: "BLOCKER RE-CHECKED 2026-08-05 at the owner question (did section 3a not finish?). Two-part answer. (1) SECTION 3a IS NOT FINISHED: it ships CONFIRM-ONLY - it confirms a data dependence and never refutes one, so inclusion is still decided by call-graph BFS. That is why INV-sadah is still violated and WI-kabif still todo_hard, and PR #204 made it machine-readable as the declared constant inclusion_decided_by = call_graph_reachability. (2) BUT THIS ITEM DOES NOT NEED THE REFUTATION ARM, AND ITS STATED BLOCKER IS NOW STALE. What it needs is statement ordering INSIDE the seed function, and that landed separately as stmt_defuse in PR #203 (INV-sadah), verified live at 13,930 functions and 144,070 statement rows on pretix. The DATA now exists; it does not reach the place that needs it. MEASURED IN CODE TODAY: the seed exemption is unchanged and live at taint.py:1709 - if taint_label in node_sanitizers and node != seed_id - inside _reachability_past_sanitizers, a SHARED helper with exactly two callers (the structural and DDG propagators). That helper receives NO statement data at all, and stmt_defuse is a parameter of propagate_taint_ddg ONLY (taint.py:2082); propagate_taint_structural has no statement ordering whatsoever. RE-SCOPED BLOCKER: thread statement ordering into the shared barrier so a sanitizer preceding the source in the seed function is honoured - possible for the DDG pass NOW - AND disclose that the STRUCTURAL pass cannot honour same-function sanitization at all, because it has no ordering to reason with. That second half is a permanent scope limit for any language without a DDG, not a deferral, and it should be stated rather than left implicit. Do NOT wait for section 3a refutation before working this. PROCESS NOTE: the first attempt to record this failed because I fabricated an 8-segment id rather than looking it up (L40), and it was caught only by reading the item back."  # 29b9
